Subject: EFA endorses ERR as a working project
Date: Sat, 15 Apr 1995 22:47:25 +1100
Message-ID: <D9xZl8ricHF8072yn@apanix.apana.org.au>

On Friday 14th April, Electronic Frontiers Australia endorsed the
Electronic Rights and Responsibilities document as a working project.
The ERR is being developed by Peter Merel <pete@extro.su.oz.au> and is
currently under discussion on the following newsgroups:

  comp.org.eff.talk, comp.org.cpsr.talk, gnu.misc.discuss,
  alt.comp.acad-freedom.talk, aus.org.efa, aus.general

The purpose of the ERR is that it be used as an ethical standard with
which to measure the policies of states and corporations with regard to
multicast communications networks.

In endorsing the ERR as a working project what EFA has done is to
endorse the concept of an ERR document.  EFA has yet to endorse the
document itself.

As a next step EFA is inviting other EF (like) groups to endorse the
concept of an ERR document and send comments to EFA within 30 days.  The
main thing EFA needs to know at this stage is what criteria will be used
to decide if the final document is acceptable.  EFA will pass these
comments on to Peter Merel who is writing the document.  Any suggestions
on how to get the document into a state where as many EF (like) groups
as possible are willing to endorse it will also be most welcome.

The latest version the ERR is available from:

   http://www.usyd.edu.au/~pete/err.html

Michael.
