	The problem isn't the difference between the mediums. The problem is
that the laws that now apply to telephone calls- restricting "obscene" or 
"indecent" material- are themselves ridiculous and unconstitutional. There is
no legitimate reason to extend these laws.
	This is an example of your most persistent and fallacious line of
argument. You have proved to us many times that speech *is* regulated now. This
is not news! You have never, however, provided a cogent argument that it
*should* be regulated, or that the government can, over the long term, be
*trusted* to regulate it. IMO, we should consider all speech regulations not by
the standard of "what is our gov't doing with them now?" but "what *could* a
tyrannical, totally amoral gov't do with them if it really wanted to?" To
paraphrase an old axiom, if you would have freedom, prepare for tyranny.

